OL,3,AMining giant joins fight to stop killer
OL,4,Atoad march across Australia
OL,5,
OL,6,FRio Tinto is ploughing millions of
OL,7,Fdollars into stopping the poisonous
OL,8,Fcane toad reaching the Pilbara region
OL,9,Fof western Australia, where the mining
OL,10,Fgiant has a vast iron ore operation.
OL,12,FThe firm, alongside Curtin University
OL,13,Fin Perth and others, will spend A$28m
OL,14,F(#14.5m) building a "toad containment
OL,15,Fzone" to prevent the pest travelling
OL,16,Fsouth.
OL,18,FWhile the cane toad is not a direct
OL,19,Fthreat to Rio Tinto's business, it
OL,20,Fproduces toxins lethal to native
OL,21,Fwildlife and poses a threat to
OL,22,FPilbara's ecosystem.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
FL,114,105,200,300,0,100
